1
00:00:05,602 --> 00:00:07,873
When did it start? When will it end?

2
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:10,377
Where did it come from,
and where did it go?

3
00:00:11,185 --> 00:00:13,609
These are the questions
we ask about anything.

4
00:00:14,429 --> 00:00:18,574
Nāgārjuna opens his verses on
the Middle Way with a homage.

5
00:00:18,654 --> 00:00:22,338
In it he names eight extremes,
set out in four pairs.

6
00:00:22,418 --> 00:00:24,199
Arising and ceasing.

7
00:00:24,279 --> 00:00:27,501
Permanence and annihilation.
Coming and going.

8
00:00:27,581 --> 00:00:29,557
Identity and difference.

9
00:00:30,369 --> 00:00:34,637
Under the logic of substance, the
view that things stand on their own,

10
00:00:34,717 --> 00:00:36,688
these are not extremes at all.

11
00:00:36,768 --> 00:00:38,604
They are simply what one asks.

12
00:00:38,684 --> 00:00:41,036
Does it last, or is it destroyed?

13
00:00:41,116 --> 00:00:43,744
Is it the same as that, or something else?

14
00:00:44,557 --> 00:00:48,281
Look closely, and each question
assumes the same thing.

15
00:00:48,361 --> 00:00:50,822
It assumes there is
something with whereabouts.

16
00:00:50,902 --> 00:00:54,517
A place in time, in space or in identity,

17
00:00:54,597 --> 00:00:57,103
that belongs to it from its own side.

18
00:00:57,905 --> 00:01:01,928
Arising and ceasing put the
thing at the two ends of a line.

19
00:01:02,008 --> 00:01:03,817
Permanence keeps it on the line.

20
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:05,569
Annihilation removes it.

21
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:08,735
Coming and going move it
from one place to another.

22
00:01:08,815 --> 00:01:13,490
Identity and difference set it beside
something else, to be compared.

23
00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:16,344
So the extremes are not
eight separate errors.

24
00:01:16,424 --> 00:01:19,120
They are eight ways of
asking where a thing is.

25
00:01:19,941 --> 00:01:23,475
The logic of dependency does
not give subtler answers.

26
00:01:23,555 --> 00:01:25,282
It turns the questions over.

27
00:01:25,362 --> 00:01:28,638
It does not say the thing
arises in some hidden form,

28
00:01:28,718 --> 00:01:30,948
or slips away somewhere invisible.

29
00:01:31,028 --> 00:01:34,861
It says that what was supposed
to have whereabouts is not found.

30
00:01:34,941 --> 00:01:37,392
And so the questions lose their object.

31
00:01:38,222 --> 00:01:41,852
Take them one by one. Ask when
something came into being.

32
00:01:41,932 --> 00:01:46,213
No thing is found crossing an
edge, from absent to present.

33
00:01:46,293 --> 00:01:50,398
Yet "it began at noon"
still holds, as convention.

34
00:01:50,478 --> 00:01:52,110
Ask when it went out of being.

35
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:54,487
No thing is found falling into nothing.

36
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:57,766
Ending is named within
a before and an after.

37
00:01:58,589 --> 00:02:00,696
Ask what stays the same underneath.

38
00:02:00,776 --> 00:02:04,827
No carrier is found beneath the
change. Ask what was destroyed.

39
00:02:04,907 --> 00:02:07,440
Nothing stood on its own to be destroyed.

40
00:02:08,241 --> 00:02:12,087
Ask where it came from. There are
no whereabouts before it appeared.

41
00:02:12,167 --> 00:02:15,172
Ask where it went. There
are no whereabouts after.

42
00:02:15,252 --> 00:02:17,323
The question simply does not apply.

43
00:02:18,133 --> 00:02:21,694
Ask whether it is the same
as its source. It is not.

44
00:02:21,774 --> 00:02:23,542
The sprout is not the seed.

45
00:02:23,622 --> 00:02:28,832
Ask whether it is something else entirely.
It is not that either. Rice yields rice.

46
00:02:29,646 --> 00:02:32,406
The decisive point is easy to miss.

47
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:37,039
Dependent arising, things coming
about through causes and conditions,

48
00:02:37,119 --> 00:02:40,572
is not one thing, and the
eight negations another.

49
00:02:40,652 --> 00:02:43,887
It is not as if what arises
in dependence were then,

50
00:02:43,967 --> 00:02:47,406
mysteriously, also free of arising.

51
00:02:47,486 --> 00:02:50,929
The negations describe
dependent arising itself.

52
00:02:51,741 --> 00:02:54,840
If a sprout could be found
arising from its seed,

53
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:57,191
it would have an arising of its own.

54
00:02:57,271 --> 00:02:59,079
Then it would not need to depend.

55
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:03,617
That it depends is exactly why no
arising is found when it is sought.

56
00:03:03,697 --> 00:03:07,381
Dependence and unfindability are one fact.

57
00:03:07,461 --> 00:03:10,750
Seen from the side of
convention, it is dependence.

58
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:14,586
Seen from the side of
analysis, it is unfindability.

59
00:03:15,409 --> 00:03:18,834
This turns ordinary
experience upside down,

60
00:03:18,914 --> 00:03:20,537
and removes none of it.

61
00:03:21,354 --> 00:03:27,008
Switch off a lamp. The room is dark, and
the light went nowhere. Switch it on.

62
00:03:27,088 --> 00:03:30,531
The room fills, and the
light came from nowhere.

63
00:03:31,366 --> 00:03:34,303
Both descriptions hold
of every appearance.

64
00:03:34,383 --> 00:03:36,182
Both were true all along.

